{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat apps/desktop/src/shell/appearance.ts apps/desktop/src/styles/tokens.css docs/architecture/desktop-themes.md'","aggregated_output":"import { GENERAL_THEMES, applyThemeAttribute, type GeneralThemeId } from '@ai-security-academy/presentation'\nimport type { ColorTheme, Theme } from '@prisma-airs/desktop-contracts'\n\n/** Maps the desktop preference to a general shared theme (never an earned skin). */\nexport function resolveTheme(theme: Theme, prefersDark: boolean): GeneralThemeId {\n    if (theme === 'light') return GENERAL_THEMES.light\n    if (theme === 'dark') return GENERAL_THEMES.dark\n    return prefersDark ? GENERAL_THEMES.dark : GENERAL_THEMES.light\n}\n\nconst darkQuery = () =>\n    typeof window.matchMedia === 'function'\n        ? window.matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)')\n        : null\n\n/** Applies the preference now and follows OS changes while it is `system`. */\nexport function followAppearance(theme: Theme, colorTheme: ColorTheme = 'prismaAirs'): () => void {\n    const query = darkQuery()\n    const apply = () => {\n        const general = resolveTheme(theme, query?.matches ?? true)\n        // Academy keeps its general palette, including portals attached to body.\n        applyThemeAttribute(general)\n        document.documentElement.dataset.appearance = general === GENERAL_THEMES.dark ? 'dark' : 'light'\n        document.documentElement.dataset.colorTheme = colorTheme\n    }\n    apply()\n    if (theme !== 'system' || !query) return () => undefined\n    query.addEventListener('change', apply)\n    return () => query.removeEventListener('change', apply)\n}\n/*\n * Desktop tokens: independent palette family and light/dark appearance.\n * Light/dark mode and the selected family paint --v2-* tokens. Root\n * data-theme keeps Academy's existing general palette. Shared controls\n * receive desktop aliases only inside explicit data-desktop-theme scopes.\n */\n:root {\n    --v2-color-scheme: light;\n    --v2-bg: #f5f6f8;\n    --v2-side: #eef0f3;\n    --v2-paper: #ffffff;\n    --v2-inset: #e9edf2;\n    --v2-rule: #d4d9e1;\n    --v2-ctl: #7b8494;\n    --v2-ink: #17212f;\n    --v2-soft: #435166;\n    --v2-faint: #5c687b;\n    --v2-acc: #b83b16;\n    --v2-acc-ink: #ffffff;\n    --v2-acc-soft: #fce6de;\n    --v2-block: #b42318;\n    --v2-block-bg: #fbe4e1;\n    --v2-flag: #815200;\n    --v2-flag-bg: #fff0c9;\n    --v2-ok: #1a6b40;\n    --v2-ok-bg: #def3e6;\n    --v2-sel: var(--v2-acc);\n    --v2-sel-ink: var(--v2-acc-ink);\n    --v2-get: #245e8f;\n\n    --v2-page-top: 32px;\n    --v2-page-x: 44px;\n    --v2-title: 26px;\n    --v2-card-pad: 20px;\n    /* Grid and card gaps (the prototype's 16–20px; 12px is only inside rows). */\n    --v2-gap: 16px;\n    --v2-gap-row: 12px;\n    /* The prototype's base text is 13px; 14px is the subtitle size. */\n    --v2-text: 13px;\n    --v2-text-1: 14px;\n    --v2-text-2: 12px;\n    --v2-h2: 13px;\n    --v2-control: 32px;\n    --v2-radius-control: 7px;\n    --v2-radius-card: 12px;\n    --v2-rail: 244px;\n    --v2-header: 56px;\n    --v2-reading: 860px;\n    /* Overlay widths (R2App): tenant menu, palette, review sheet, detail sheet, dialogs. */\n    --v2-menu: 360px;\n    --v2-palette: 640px;\n    --v2-sheet: 620px;\n    --v2-detail: 520px;\n    --v2-dialog: 560px;\n    --v2-scrim: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.22);\n    --v2-scrim-deep: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.34);\n}\n\n:root[data-appearance='dark'] {\n    --v2-color-scheme: dark;\n    --v2-bg: #151b25;\n    --v2-side: #101620;\n    --v2-paper: #1e2734;\n    --v2-inset: #263243;\n    --v2-rule: #37465b;\n    --v2-ctl: #8190a5;\n    --v2-ink: #f0f3f8;\n    --v2-soft: #c7d0dd;\n    --v2-faint: #aab8cb;\n    --v2-acc: #ff9a70;\n    --v2-acc-ink: #26190f;\n    --v2-acc-soft: #4b2e25;\n    --v2-block: #ff9b94;\n    --v2-block-bg: #492a31;\n    --v2-flag: #f7c567;\n    --v2-flag-bg: #40351e;\n    --v2-ok: #8ddbb1;\n    --v2-ok-bg: #1a3d32;\n    --v2-get: #8cc8ff;\n}\n\n:root[data-color-theme='gruvbox'][data-appearance='light'] {\n    --v2-color-scheme: light;\n    --v2-bg: #fbf1c7;\n    --v2-side: #f2e5bc;\n    --v2-paper: #fff8df;\n    --v2-inset: #ebdbb2;\n    --v2-rule: #d5c4a1;\n    --v2-ctl: #85745b;\n    --v2-ink: #282828;\n    --v2-soft: #504945;\n    --v2-faint: #665c54;\n    --v2-acc: #a3390c;\n    --v2-acc-ink: #ffffff;\n    --v2-acc-soft: #f5d7ac;\n    --v2-block: #9d201b;\n    --v2-block-bg: #f8d7c3;\n    --v2-flag: #785500;\n    --v2-flag-bg: #f5e4a9;\n    --v2-ok: #426421;\n    --v2-ok-bg: #e3ebbb;\n    --v2-get: #076678;\n}\n\n:root[data-color-theme='gruvbox'][data-appearance='dark'] {\n    --v2-color-scheme: dark;\n    --v2-bg: #1d2021;\n    --v2-side: #161919;\n    --v2-paper: #282828;\n    --v2-inset: #32302f;\n    --v2-rule: #3c3836;\n    --v2-ctl: #8a7f70;\n    --v2-ink: #ebdbb2;\n    --v2-soft: #d5c4a1;\n    --v2-faint: #bdae93;\n    --v2-acc: #fe8019;\n    --v2-acc-ink: #1d2021;\n    --v2-acc-soft: #4a2f1a;\n    --v2-block: #ff6b57;\n    --v2-block-bg: #3d1f1c;\n    --v2-flag: #fabd2f;\n    --v2-flag-bg: #3a3019;\n    --v2-ok: #b8bb26;\n    --v2-ok-bg: #2b2f17;\n    --v2-get: #83a598;\n}\n\n/* The v2 shell root: body background, type and the visible focus ring\n * (invariant: accent-colour ring on every focusable control; inset variant\n * where a control declares it). */\n[data-v2-shell] {\n    background: var(--v2-bg);\n    color: var(--v2-ink);\n    font-size: var(--v2-text);\n    font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'SF Pro Text', system-ui, sans-serif;\n    min-height: 100vh;\n}\n/* The destination heading takes focus after navigation for assistive technology; it is not a control, so no ring (C35). */\n[data-v2-shell] h1[tabindex='-1']:focus {\n    outline: none;\n}\n/* A page inside the shell's main region: the prototype's 32/44 margins, scrolling by itself. */\n[data-v2-shell] [data-v2-page] {\n    padding: var(--v2-page-top) var(--v2-page-x) 28px;\n    overflow-y: auto;\n    min-height: 0;\n    flex-grow: 1;\n    min-width: 0;\n}\n/* Shell ancestry includes Academy; desktop control styling needs ownership. */\n[data-desktop-theme] :focus-visible {\n    outline: 2px solid var(--v2-acc);\n    outline-offset: 2px;\n}\n[data-desktop-theme] [data-inset-focus]:focus-visible {\n    outline-offset: -4px;\n}\n[data-desktop-theme] input,\n[data-desktop-theme] select,\n[data-desktop-theme] textarea {\n    border: 1px solid var(--v2-ctl);\n    border-radius: var(--v2-radius-control);\n    background: var(--v2-bg);\n    color: var(--v2-ink);\n    min-height: var(--v2-control);\n}\n/* Rail collapses to icons below 1280 CSS px; nothing scrolls horizontally. */\n[data-v2-shell] {\n    overflow-x: hidden;\n}\n@media (max-width: 1279px) {\n    [data-v2-rail] {\n        width: 64px !important;\n    }\n    /* Collapsed: one 32px control per row; icons stay, labels leave the\n     * layout but stay in the accessible name. */\n    [data-v2-rail] [data-v2-stack] {\n        flex-direction: column;\n        align-items: stretch;\n    }\n    [data-v2-rail] [data-v2-stack] > * {\n        width: 100%;\n    }\n    /* Collapsed: labels leave the layout but stay in the accessible name (rail and header). */\n    [data-v2-rail] [data-v2-label],\n    [data-v2-header] [data-v2-label] {\n        position: absolute;\n        width: 1px;\n        height: 1px;\n        overflow: hidden;\n        clip: rect(0 0 0 0);\n        white-space: nowrap;\n    }\n    /* Collapsed: the product children and the status rows leave the rail (C35). */\n    [data-v2-rail] [data-v2-collapse] {\n        display: none !important;\n    }\n    [data-v2-rail] [data-v2-stack] > * {\n        padding-left: 0 !important;\n        padding-right: 0 !important;\n    }\n    [data-v2-header] [data-v2-search] {\n        width: auto !important;\n        flex: 1 1 120px !important;\n        min-width: 0;\n    }\n    /* The Harness's rail and Decisions aside stack above and below the transcript when the page is narrow (C38).\n       Wide, the columns are one flex line bounded by the page, so each column scrolls on its own. */\n    [data-v2-shell] [data-slot='harness-columns'] {\n        flex-wrap: wrap;\n    }\n    [data-v2-shell] [data-slot='harness-rail'],\n    [data-v2-shell] [data-slot='harness-decisions'] {\n        flex: 1 1 100% !important;\n        border-left: 0 !important;\n        border-right: 0 !important;\n        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--v2-rule);\n    }\n    /* Home's attention and quick-action sections stack when the page is narrow (C36). */\n    [data-v2-shell] [data-slot='home-lower'] {\n        grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) !important;\n    }\n}\n/* The Harness composer is one pill: the ring is the pill's when its box is typed in (C38). */\n[data-v2-shell] [data-slot='harness-composer']:focus-within {\n    outline: 2px solid var(--v2-acc);\n    outline-offset: 1px;\n}\n[data-v2-shell] [data-slot='harness-composer'] textarea:focus-visible {\n    outline: none;\n}\n/* The selected sidebar destination is accent-filled, so its ring is the\n * ink-on-accent colour; every other control keeps the accent ring, including\n * a current link on an accent-soft surface (the Academy's section links: the\n * accent is 5.05:1 on the light soft surface and 4.86:1 on the dark one, where\n * the ink-on-accent colour was 1.06:1 and 1.11:1). */\n[data-desktop-theme] [data-inset-focus][aria-current='page']:focus-visible {\n    outline-color: var(--v2-sel-ink);\n}\n[data-v2-shell] [data-v2-scrim] {\n    background: var(--v2-scrim);\n}\n@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {\n    [data-v2-shell] * {\n        transition: none !important;\n        animation: none !important;\n    }\n}\n\n/* C41 API Client: the pretty JSON view numbers its lines from a counter (the numbers are not part of the body's text). */\n[data-v2-shell] [data-slot='json-lines'] {\n    counter-reset: line;\n    white-space: pre;\n}\n[data-v2-shell] [data-slot='json-lines'] > [data-line]::before {\n    counter-increment: line;\n    content: counter(line);\n    display: inline-block;\n    width: 34px;\n    padding-right: 12px;\n    text-align: right;\n    color: var(--v2-faint);\n}\n/* The request's columns and the response pane stack below the width that fits them (the prototype is fixed-width). */\n@media (max-width: 1180px) {\n    [data-v2-shell] [data-slot='workbench-columns'] {\n        flex-wrap: wrap;\n    }\n    [data-v2-shell] [data-slot='workbench-response-pane'] {\n        flex: 1 1 100% !important;\n        max-width: none !important;\n        border-top: 1px solid var(--v2-rule);\n    }\n}\n/* The wizard's product cards (C43): the card is a label around a visually hidden native checkbox; the card shows\n   the control's focus ring and its chosen state. */\n[data-slot='product-card']:has(> input:focus-visible) {\n    outline: 2px solid var(--v2-acc);\n    outline-offset: 2px;\n}\n/* The wizard (C43) below 760px (a 900-point window at 200%): the rail is a compact strip above the step (the step\n   marks keep their names for assistive technology but show their numbers), every grid is one column, and the step\n   scrolls between the strip and the pinned footer. */\n@media (max-width: 760px) {\n    [data-v2-shell] [data-slot='wizard'],\n    [data-slot='wizard'] {\n        flex-direction: column;\n    }\n    [data-slot='wizard'] > nav {\n        width: 100% !important;\n        flex: 0 0 auto;\n        padding: 10px 12px 8px !important;\n        border-right: 0 !important;\n        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--v2-rule);\n    }\n    [data-slot='wizard'] > nav > div:first-child {\n        margin-bottom: 8px !important;\n    }\n    [data-slot='wizard'] > nav > ol {\n        flex-direction: row;\n        flex-wrap: wrap;\n        gap: 4px !important;\n    }\n    [data-slot='wizard'] > nav > ol button {\n        width: auto;\n        height: 32px !important;\n        padding: 0 6px !important;\n        gap: 0 !important;\n    }\n    [data-slot='wizard'] > nav > ol button > span:not(:first-child) {\n        position: absolute;\n        width: 1px;\n        height: 1px;\n        overflow: hidden;\n        clip: rect(0 0 0 0);\n        white-space: nowrap;\n    }\n    [data-slot='wizard'] > nav > [data-slot='privacy-note'] {\n        display: none;\n    }\n    [data-slot='wizard'] > nav > [data-slot='theme-button'] {\n        margin-top: 6px !important;\n    }\n    [data-slot='wizard'] main .grid {\n        grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) !important;\n    }\n    /* The strip drops the brand row (the sheet is already named), and the footer's hint or status keeps to two\n       lines: at 900×600 and 200% the add sheet is 279 CSS px tall, and a long hint made the footer taller than the\n       sheet, pushing its primary below the window. */\n    [data-slot='wizard'] > nav > div:first-child {\n        display: none;\n    }\n    [data-slot='wizard-footer'] [data-slot='wizard-status'] > span {\n        display: -webkit-box;\n        -webkit-line-clamp: 2;\n        -webkit-box-orient: vertical;\n        overflow: hidden;\n    }\n}\n@media (max-width: 1279px) {\n    [data-v2-rail] {\n        width: 64px !important;\n    }\n    /* Collapsed: one 32px control per row; icons stay, labels leave the\n     * layout but stay in the accessible name. */\n    [data-v2-rail] [data-v2-stack] {\n        flex-direction: column;\n        align-items: stretch;\n    }\n    [data-v2-rail] [data-v2-stack] > * {\n        width: 100%;\n    }\n    /* Collapsed: labels leave the layout but stay in the accessible name (rail and header). */\n    [data-v2-rail] [data-v2-label],\n    [data-v2-header] [data-v2-label] {\n        position: absolute;\n        width: 1px;\n        height: 1px;\n        overflow: hidden;\n        clip: rect(0 0 0 0);\n        white-space: nowrap;\n    }\n    /* Collapsed: the product children and the status rows leave the rail (C35). */\n    [data-v2-rail] [data-v2-collapse] {\n        display: none !important;\n    }\n    [data-v2-rail] [data-v2-stack] > * {\n        padding-left: 0 !important;\n        padding-right: 0 !important;\n    }\n    [data-v2-header] [data-v2-search] {\n        width: auto !important;\n        flex: 1 1 120px !important;\n        min-width: 0;\n    }\n    /* The Harness's rail and Decisions aside stack above and below the transcript when the page is narrow (C38).\n       Wide, the columns are one flex line bounded by the page, so each column scrolls on its own. */\n    [data-v2-shell] [data-slot='harness-columns'] {\n        flex-wrap: wrap;\n    }\n    [data-v2-shell] [data-slot='harness-rail'],\n    [data-v2-shell] [data-slot='harness-decisions'] {\n        flex: 1 1 100% !important;\n        border-left: 0 !important;\n        border-right: 0 !important;\n        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--v2-rule);\n    }\n    /* Home's attention and quick-action sections stack when the page is narrow (C36). */\n    [data-v2-shell] [data-slot='home-lower'] {\n        grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) !important;\n    }\n    /* The Inbox's list and detail cards stack when the page is narrow (C37): each card takes its\n       own height (the list up to half the viewport, scrolling inside) and the page scrolls. */\n    [data-v2-shell] [data-slot='inbox-columns'] {\n        grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) !important;\n        grid-template-rows: auto auto;\n        min-height: auto !important;\n        flex-grow: 0 !important;\n    }\n    [data-v2-shell] [data-slot='inbox-list'] {\n        min-height: 240px;\n        max-height: 50vh;\n    }\n}\n/* C39a attempt-01 R1: below the width that fits the inventory's columns (900×600 at 200% is 450 CSS px) the rows stack their cells. */\n@media (max-width: 760px) {\n    [data-v2-shell] [data-slot='administration-row'] {\n        grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) !important;\n        gap: 4px !important;\n    }\n    /* The header row leaves the picture but not the accessibility tree; each stacked cell shows its column's\n       name (C39b attempt-01 R4). */\n    [data-v2-shell] [data-slot='administration-table'] > [role='row']:first-child {\n        position: absolute;\n        width: 1px;\n        height: 1px;\n        overflow: hidden;\n        clip: rect(0 0 0 0);\n        white-space: nowrap;\n    }\n    [data-v2-shell] [data-slot='administration-row'] > [role='cell'][data-label]::before {\n        content: attr(data-label) ': ';\n        font-weight: 600;\n        color: var(--v2-faint);\n    }\n    [data-v2-shell] [data-slot='administration-row'] > [role='cell']:last-child {\n        justify-content: flex-start;\n    }\n}\n/* C39b attempt-01: below the width that fits a table's columns (900×600 at 200% is 450 CSS px) the v2 admin tables stack their cells and hide the header row. */\n@media (max-width: 760px) {\n    [data-v2-shell] [data-slot='admin-tab'] [role='table'] > [role='row'] {\n        grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) !important;\n        gap: 4px !important;\n    }\n    [data-v2-shell] [data-slot='admin-tab'] [role='table'] > [role='row']:first-child {\n        display: none;\n    }\n    [data-v2-shell] [data-slot='admin-tab'] [role='table'] [role='cell'] {\n        white-space: normal;\n    }\n}\n/* Narrower still (a 900-point window at 200%): the request tree sits above the editor instead of beside it. */\n@media (max-width: 760px) {\n    [data-v2-shell] [data-slot='api-body'] {\n        flex-wrap: wrap;\n    }\n    [data-v2-shell] [data-slot='request-tree'] {\n        width: 100% !important;\n        max-height: 40vh;\n        border-right: 0 !important;\n        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--v2-rule);\n    }\n}\n/* Test Cases (C40): below 760px (a 900-point window at 200%) each row is two lines: the case and its product, the\n   input, then the result and the action; the five-column grid cannot hold readable cells there. */\n@media (max-width: 760px) {\n    [data-v2-shell] [data-slot='cases-table'] [role='row'] {\n        grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto !important;\n        row-gap: 8px !important;\n    }\n    [data-v2-shell] [data-slot='cases-table'] [role='row'] > :nth-child(3) {\n        grid-column: 1 / -1;\n    }\n}\n/* The wizard's Environment segmented control (C43): native radios inside labels; the segment shows the ring. */\n[data-slot='environment-choice']:has(> input:focus-visible) {\n    outline: 2px solid var(--v2-acc);\n    outline-offset: 1px;\n}\n\n/* Shared controls follow the desktop palette only in explicitly owned scopes.\n * Academy and its body portals retain the general root palette. */\n[data-desktop-theme] {\n    color-scheme: var(--v2-color-scheme);\n    --academy-bg: var(--v2-bg);\n    --academy-bg-rail: var(--v2-side);\n    --academy-bg-inset: var(--v2-inset);\n    --academy-paper: var(--v2-paper);\n    --academy-paper-deep: var(--v2-inset);\n    --academy-ink: var(--v2-ink);\n    --academy-ink-soft: var(--v2-soft);\n    --academy-ink-faint: var(--v2-faint);\n    --academy-rule: var(--v2-rule);\n    --academy-rule-strong: var(--v2-ctl);\n    --academy-track: var(--v2-rule);\n    --academy-accent: var(--v2-acc);\n    --academy-accent-ink: var(--v2-acc-ink);\n    --academy-accent-soft: var(--v2-acc-soft);\n    --academy-accent-ring: var(--v2-acc);\n    --academy-focus-ring: var(--v2-acc);\n    --academy-accent-warn: var(--v2-block);\n    --academy-saved-dot: var(--v2-ok);\n    --academy-info: var(--v2-get);\n    --academy-active-chip: var(--v2-inset);\n}\n\n.settings-grid {\n    display: grid;\n    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 23rem), 1fr));\n    gap: 16px;\n    align-items: start;\n}\n.settings-card {\n    min-width: 0;\n    display: flex;\n    flex-direction: column;\n    gap: 12px;\n    padding: 16px;\n    border: 1px solid var(--v2-rule);\n    border-radius: var(--v2-radius-card);\n    background: var(--v2-paper);\n    color: var(--v2-ink);\n    font-size: 13px;\n}\n.settings-card > legend, .settings-card > h3 {\n    padding: 0 4px;\n    font-size: 14px;\n    font-weight: 600;\n}\n.settings-description { color: var(--v2-soft); font-size: 12px; }\n.settings-fields {\n    display: grid;\n    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 12rem), 1fr));\n    gap: 12px;\n}\n.settings-field { display: flex; min-width: 0; flex-direction: column; gap: 5px; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 500; }\n.settings-card :is(input:not([type='radio']):not([type='checkbox']), select) {\n    width: 100%; min-width: 0; min-height: 32px; padding: 5px 9px; font-size: 13px;\n}\n.settings-card :is(button, [type='radio'], [type='checkbox']) { flex-shrink: 0; }\n.settings-card button { min-height: 32px; height: auto; padding-top: 5px; padding-bottom: 5px; }\n# Desktop color themes\n\nThe desktop owns two independent preferences: appearance (`system`, `light`,\n`dark`) and color theme (`prismaAirs`, `gruvbox`). Prisma AIRS is the default.\nNeither preference updates an Academy account or unlocks an earned cosmetic.\n\nExisting state without `colorTheme` defaults to Prisma AIRS and retains its\nappearance. The default is omitted when saving; an alternate theme is saved as\nan explicit field. Invalid theme values remain a storage error, rather than\nsilently overwriting the preference. Existing atomic storage writes apply.\n\nOlder binaries use strict field validation and can reject state written with a\nnew preference. Opening an upgraded data directory with an older release is\nunsupported; this change does not claim downgrade compatibility or silently\nreset data. Preserve the state before any explicitly requested downgrade.\n\nThe document's general Academy theme continues to follow appearance. Desktop\npalette tokens are independent, and shared presentation colors are adapted only\ninside desktop theme scopes. Academy content and its portals keep the general\nAcademy palette. Earned Academy themes remain under Academy's existing rules.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
